msgid "Hades is in an elliptic orbit around Apollo, its star, with a low orbital eccentricity. When you follow Apollo in the sky throughout the year, you will see how Apollo will notably change in its apparent size. On Summer Solstice, Apollo appears about twice at large in the sky than on New Year’s Day."
